r2 findings remain open/partial: **#1, #2, #3 (J1 only), #5, #6, #13, #14**. Findings **#4, #7–#12, #15–#19** are 
resolved in v2. D1–D4 are accepted. All 32 Must FRs and 16 BRs have AC links; the semantic coverage gaps below remain.

1. **High — FR-004–006/009, AC-041–042: absence does not prove safe cancellation or takeover.** A closed tab’s 
accepted create can remain blocked before INSERT. Lookup returns absent, another tab cancels/expires/resends, then the 
original create commits. The existing repository separates lookup from INSERT ([SupabaseMessageRepository.ts:530](/E:/p
rojects/virtual-office/src/repositories/implementations/supabase/SupabaseMessageRepository.ts:530)). A live but hung 
owner can also block recovery indefinitely. 
[SPEC:96](/E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md:96). **Fix:** require 
server-fenced attempt ownership and bounded recovery; unknown becomes waiting only when no previous attempt can still 
commit. Test with the original INSERT blocked in real Postgres through lookup, cancellation, and takeover. **r2 #2/#5 
remain partial.**

2. **High — FR-001 versus §11/AC-039: IndexedDB failure bypasses durability.** The Phase 4 fallback permits dispatch 
without durable storage, reopening the original close-before-response loss window. Phase 4 keeps the key in a 
component ref and uses plain fetch 
([message-composer.tsx:145](/E:/projects/virtual-office/src/components/messaging/message-composer.tsx:145), 
[messaging-api.ts:131](/E:/projects/virtual-office/src/lib/messaging-api.ts:131)). 
[SPEC:196](/E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md:196). **Fix:** “If the 
durable write fails, do not dispatch or clear the composer; retain the composition with an actionable storage 
failure.” AC-039 must inject storage failure with HTTP working and assert zero create requests. **r2 #1 remains 
partial.**

3. **High — FR-024/025, §12, AC-024/026: send-time membership does not authorize later notification.** AC-024 tests 
someone already outside the conversation. It misses removal after commit but before enrichment/notification completes, 
and account switching during that wait. The existing handler already awaits a claim before displaying content 
([use-message-notifications.ts:124](/E:/projects/virtual-office/src/hooks/ui/use-message-notifications.ts:124)). 
[SPEC:217](/E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md:217). **Fix:** fence 
pending notifications by current identity and membership generation, require current authorization before emission, 
and discard work on removal/switch. Add delayed-delivery E2Es; link removal coverage to R1-q16 F.

4. **Medium — FR-011, AC-012/013/044: late completions remain untested.** AC-044 pauses before dispatch; AC-013 stops 
drains but never releases a late success/error afterward. Existing completions write to conversation-only cache keys 
([useMessages.ts:317](/E:/projects/virtual-office/src/hooks/useMessages.ts:317)). 
[SPEC:275](/E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md:275). **Fix:** add E2Es 
releasing real create and lookup responses after A→C and confirmed logout. Assert no old content enters C’s view, no 
deleted item reappears, and stale completions cannot modify replacement claims. **r2 #6 remains partial.**

5. **Medium — FR-002/004, BR-003, AC-005: per-item claims do not validate conversation-wide serialization.** Two tabs 
can claim different keys in one conversation concurrently and still satisfy AC-005’s per-key exclusivity and 
uniqueness assertions. 
[SPEC:236](/E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md:236). **Fix:** require a 
shared durable ordering and atomic eligibility of only the oldest unresolved item across all tabs. Hold m1’s real 
request while another tab attempts m2; assert no overlap and original delivery order.

6. **Medium — G2, FR-001/002, AC-005/038/040: pending-to-stored UI correlation is unspecified.** Current message 
types/mappers omit `clientMessageId`; optimistic matching guesses from content and timestamps within one second 
([message-cache.ts:28](/E:/projects/virtual-office/src/lib/messaging/message-cache.ts:28)). That cannot reliably 
reconcile long-queued or identical messages before the HTTP response arrives. 
[SPEC:93](/E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md:93). **Fix:** require stable 
key-based correlation across outbox, create, lookup, feed, and Realtime representations. Test identical text with 
different reply/mention compositions, Realtime-before-response, and one bubble throughout in both sender tabs.

7. **Medium — FR-027/028, AC-028/029: metrics bounds regressed and hanging delivery is insufficiently bounded.** V1 
explicitly bounded request size and batch length ([SPEC-v1-reviewed.md:205](/E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/
phase-5-messaging-resilience/reviews/SPEC-v1-reviewed.md:205)); v2 retains only field bounds, a client buffer, and 
request-rate limiting. One enormous valid batch can flood logs. Repeated hanging batches can accumulate outside the 
buffer and consume HTTP capacity. 
[SPEC:119](/E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md:119). **Fix:** restore 
byte/event-count limits; define bounded concurrent delivery, cancellation deadlines, and overload dropping. Test 
oversized valid batches and sustained hanging traffic while messaging continues. **r2 #14 remains partial.**

8. **Medium — FR-008, AC-009, §12: quota-free replay lacks an independent abuse budget and concurrent charging rule.** 
Exact replay performs authenticated database reads/enrichment 
([create/route.ts:336](/E:/projects/virtual-office/src/app/api/messages/create/route.ts:336)). Unlimited replay/lookup 
traffic can bypass the create quota. Concurrent requests for an initially absent key can also be charged before 
becoming replays. [SPEC:100](/E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md:100). 
**Fix:** preserve D1’s exemption while adding a separate shared request budget for replay/lookup traffic. Charge 
create quota only once for the winning insertion. Test concurrent same-key requests and concurrent distinct keys at 
the quota boundary.

9. **Medium — FR-024, BR-010, AC-024: unchanged mention replay after membership changes is ambiguous.** Revalidating 
recipients on replay can turn an unchanged request into a different mention set when B has left, causing 409; FR-007 
then creates another message under a new key. 
[SPEC:116](/E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md:116). **Fix:** distinguish 
first-create recipient validation from replay comparison against immutable original composition. An unchanged replay 
must return the stored message without reinterpreting recipients. Test valid-recipient removal between creation and 
replay, while suppressing notifications to the removed recipient.

10. **Medium — FR-014–016, AC-015/016: independent health and non-degradation are not fully asserted.** AC-015 checks 
independent recovery, while AC-016 tests a combined outage and only message uniqueness during overlap. These can pass 
with message-only banner/polling health or stale polling overwriting enriched state. Existing status exposes only the 
message channel 
([MessagingContext.tsx:251](/E:/projects/virtual-office/src/contexts/messaging/MessagingContext.tsx:251)); raw events 
omit enrichment 
([useMessageSubscription.ts:48](/E:/projects/virtual-office/src/hooks/realtime/useMessageSubscription.ts:48)). 
[SPEC:246](/E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md:246). **Fix:** 
independently assert banner/polling thresholds for both required streams, and release stale polls after newer Realtime 
updates while checking attachments, mentions, reactions, receipts, and pagination. **r2 #13 remains partial.**

11. **Medium — FR-021/022 versus FR-016; J1 versus D1: deadlines conflict.** Five-second cross-device synchronization 
is unconditional, but Realtime-only failure permits no polling for 30 seconds and then 15-second intervals. J1 still 
promises every pending message within ten seconds without D1’s queue/quota conditions. 
[SPEC:77](/E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md:77), 
[SPEC:113](/E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md:113), 
[state.md:216](/E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/state.md:216). **Fix:** state 
healthy-connectivity prerequisites for the five-second target, cross-reference degraded deadlines, and copy D1’s 
qualification into J1. **r2 #3 remains open only in J1.**

12. **Medium — §14/15: AC references overstate semantic traceability.** AC-017 validates stopping/closing, but not 
leaving a conversation, so R1-q16 E is only partly covered. BR-005 lacks concrete 404/400/413/422 and 5xx outcome 
assertions. FR-024’s literal-text rule and §12’s caller-only lookup authorization lack negative acceptance cases. 
